{"title":"Lucas' Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Lucas' Theorem</b> states that for any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83de5740420ce29547ff18fa276d47cc97c96597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee5bad0ed1c37e47a183cc9bb81a0a4007fc3f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\overline{n_mn_{m-1}\\cdots n_0})_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> is the representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base\" title=\"Base\">base</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/2282f2758ad25817538004b097f2aaedcb8e7d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\overline{i_mi_{m-1}\\cdots i_0})_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" /> is the representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (possibly with some leading <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s) then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8f31901f19f87e960c86a40c65ed3a4fbc3ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{i}\\equiv \\prod_{j=0}^{m}\\binom{n_j}{i_j}\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"206\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lemma\">Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lucas%27_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f5f5ce8d0523086e70e4bf1998176da8c955f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,r\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/7931ec8ec0b821c30647d45a9013d573cf554bac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+x)^{p^r}\\equiv 1+x^{p^r}\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" /></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lucas%27_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4e3f04ea19b2b8ba3372f947a7c991e229e090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq k \\leq p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9231b2953450a4e879fd0c08d4d641927f8eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{p}{k}\\equiv 0 \\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"142\" height=\"53\" />. Then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a159b02e45999c4841f606da65af468bbd383c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}(1+x)^p&amp;\\equiv &amp;\\binom{p}{0}+\\binom{p}{1}x+\\binom{p}{2}x^2+\\cdots+\\binom{p}{p-1}x^{p-1}+\\binom{p}{p}x^p\\\\ &amp;\\equiv&amp; 1+x^p\\pmod{p}\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"539\" height=\"78\" />\nAssume we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/26237a265a6d58236c91bec4c54266c1d1bb5b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+x)^{p^k}\\equiv 1+x^{p^k}\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"22\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d2f7c93866a293d220b4d94fc5c3710328d11b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}(1+x)^{p^{k+1}} &amp;\\equiv&amp;\\left((1+x)^{p^k}\\right)^p\\\\ &amp;\\equiv&amp;\\left(1+x^{p^k}\\right)^p\\\\ &amp;\\equiv&amp;\\binom{p}{0}+\\binom{p}{1}x^{p^k}+\\binom{p}{2}x^{2p^k}+\\cdots+\\binom{p}{p-1}x^{(p-1)p^k}+\\binom{p}{p}x^{p^{k+1}}\\\\ &amp;\\equiv&amp;1+x^{p^{k+1}}\\pmod{p}\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"634\" height=\"162\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lucas%27_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combinatorics\" title=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Generating_function\" title=\"Generating function\">Generating function</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_Theorem\" title=\"Binomial Theorem\">Binomial Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNew